# ==============================================================================
# SyllabusSync AI — Frontend Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# This file documents the client-side public environment variables used by Vite.
# Copy this file to `frontend/.env` or `frontend/.env.local` for local development:
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# NOTE: In Vite, only variables prefixed with `VITE_` are exposed to client-side code.
# ==============================================================================

# Supabase Project Configuration (Client-side Public Credentials)
# These credentials are safe for public browser exposure.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL: Your Supabase Project URL (e.g. https://your-project-id.supabase.co)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co

# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Your Supabase Public Anonymous API Key (anon/public role)
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_public_anon_key_here

# ==============================================================================
# CRITICAL SECURITY GUIDELINES:
# ==============================================================================
# 1. NEVER put the Supabase service-role key (`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` or `service_role secret`)
#    in this file or any frontend code! The service-role key bypasses Row Level Security (RLS)
#    and grants full administrative access to your database.
# 2. NEVER put the Supabase JWT secret (`SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET`) in frontend environment variables.
#    The JWT secret is exclusively used by the backend to verify HS256 signatures.
# 3. VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the public client key meant for the browser.
#    It respects all Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) policies.

